	  Installing "Transmedia Pages" on your Psion 3a/3c


This product contains a directory of restaurants in the United Kingdom, 
which participate in the "Transmedia - The restaurant card (TM)" programme, 

We hope you choose to subscribe to Transmedia's restaurant card, which 
currently has in excess of half a million members, worldwide.  Doing so will 
ensure you receive a 25% saving on the food & beverage portion of your bill 
at any of Transmedia's 6,000 participating restaurants, worldwide.  An 
application form is included with all demonstration diskettes mailed.  
Alternatively, if you copied Transmedia Pages from the Internet, fill out 
the form contained in the file apply.txt and return it to Transmedia UK.  
Psion members receive quartlery, diskette based directory updates, and, for 
a limited period, also receive 6 months free subscription to Transmedia's 
restaurant card.  You can copy the supplied databases to your Psion Series 3a,  

One copy of Pages Viewer search software, is used to access any number of 
databases.   Download the file mp_view.zip for Pages Viewer.

The UK databases, and its approximate size as summarised below :

  Database name                           Size                    Code
United Kingdom restaurants                43Kb                    tmu

   
    Select the installation procedure appropriate for the technology 
	available to you, for copying information to your Psion.


1) Installation procedure  - Using PsiWin, Winlink or the MAC's Psion Link
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
This procedure assumes you know how to use standard Windows "drag & drop" 
techniques.  As you do NOT want to convert files during copying, ensure 
PsiManager has conversion disabled.  You can check this in PsiWin's Psion 
Manager by selecting "conversions" from the "setup" menu and ensuring the 
"allow convert on Drag & Drop" box is clear, ie not selected.  Connect 
the Psion 3Link serial cable between the PC and your Psion 3a.  On the Psion, 
from the System screen, use Psion-l to set 'Remote link'  to 'On' and ensure 
the 'Baud rate' is set correctly.

Copying to your Psion - Create the \app\pages directory on your Psion, if it 
doesn't exist.  Copy the files in the \app directory to a \app directory on 
any device on your Psion 3a and then copy all files in the \app\pages 
directory , to a \app\pages directory on your Psion.

Installing the software & database(s) - Use Psion-i to install the PAGESmgr 
and PAGESi icons on the System screen.  If this is the first time you have loaded Mobile Pages, simply press 'Enter' on the PAGESi icons.  This will allow you to access, search and view the database(s) you have just downloaded.  If  you have loaded a new version of software or additional databases, simply enter PAGESmgr and select 'Auto install', before entering PAGESi.


2) Installation procedure  - Using the Cyclone diskette drive
-------------------------------------------------------------
Insert the Mobile Pages diskette into the Cyclone and plug the Cyclone into 
the Psion.  Use Psion-i to install PAGESmgr from drive c: and enter PAGESmgr.

Copying the software - Select 'Software copy/download', followed by 
'Copy between Psion devices'.  Copying from C, to the device of your choice.
Copying the databases(s) - Select 'Database copy/download', followed by 
'Copy between Psion devices'. Then, for each database you want to copy, 
supply its 3 character code, and copy it from device C, to the device of 
your choice.

Installing the software & database(s) - Press Psion-/ over the PAGESmgr icon 
to deinstall PAGESmgr from drive C. Use Psion-i to install the PAGESmgr and 
PAGESi icons on the System screen.  If this is the first time you have loaded 
Mobile Pages, simply press 'Enter' on the PAGESi icons.  This will allow you 
to access, search and view the database(s) you have just downloaded.  If  you 
have loaded a new version of software or additional databases, simply enter 
PAGESmgr and select 'Auto install', before entering PAGESi.

3) Installation procedure - using RCOM or MCLINK
------------------------------------------------
Connect the Psion 3Link serial cable between the PC and your Psion 3a.  On 
the Psion, from the System screen, use Psion-l to set 'Remote link'  to 'On' 
and ensure the 'Baud rate' is set correctly.  On the PC, start RCOM or MCLINK.  
If you are installing from a diskette, simply insert the diskette into your 
PC's diskette drive.  If you are installing  from the hard disk of a PC, you 
should have selected the base directory you copied all the files into.  You 
can easily identify this directory, as it will contain this 'readme.1st' file 
and the file 'pages.ini'.

Upgrading from an earlier software revision - Revision 1 -Delete the file 
\app\pages\mp_pages.opo on your Psion.  Revision 2 - Enter PAGESmgr, select 
Software update and Prepare PC download.  Then continue with the next step.

Copying the software - Copy the file pagesmgr.opa from your PC to any \app 
directory on your Psion and use Psion-i on the Psion to install the PAGESmgr 
program. Enter PAGESmgr on the Psion., answer a few simple questions, and the 
software will be copied to the Psion.

Copying the database(s) - PAGESmgr will ask you if you want to load a 
database from the PC.  Answering "Y" (for YES) will present you with a menu 
of databases available on the PC.  Select a database, answer a few simple 
questions, and the database will be copied to the Psion.  You can repeat this 
step for every databases you want to download,  and at any time in the future, 
by simply entering PAGESmgr and selecting the appropriate option.

Installing the software & database(s) - Exit PAGESmgr and use Psion-i to 
install PAGESi.opa on your Psion.  The PAGESi icon will then appear on the 
screen.  Pressing 'Enter' on the PAGESi icon will allow you to access, search 
and view the database(s) you have just downloaded.  

